{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 1151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When people say:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144,
    "dDurationMs": 2507,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"When you sit in a chair like\nI'm sitting in this chair right now\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3650,
    "dDurationMs": 2501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I'm actually hovering over this chair\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6182,
    "dDurationMs": 4059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"but actually my butt is hovering\nabove the chair by this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10253,
    "dDurationMs": 4053,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just tiny tiny amout\"\n\"because of the electrons of my body\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14306,
    "dDurationMs": 4747,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"because the electrons of my butt\"\n\"are repelling the electrons of this chair\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19054,
    "dDurationMs": 3879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"it's not us actually touching the subatomic\nmaterial of the object\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22939,
    "dDurationMs": 5337,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that really true? Does it mean that MC Hammer\nhas just been singing about physics all along?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28282,
    "dDurationMs": 1194,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Can't touch this !!\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29463,
    "dDurationMs": 4184,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alas, this doesn't take into account the fact\nthat the universe is quantum mechanical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33657,
    "dDurationMs": 3096,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, you probably know that electrons\nbehave like spread-out waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36781,
    "dDurationMs": 1826,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and from chemistry, you probably also know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38637,
    "dDurationMs": 2414,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it's perfectly fine for two\nnegatively charged electrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41072,
    "dDurationMs": 2479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to share the same energy level\nof an atom or a molecule"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43582,
    "dDurationMs": 3488,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as long as they have their intrinsic spins\noriented in opposite directions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47075,
    "dDurationMs": 2134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, even though electrons repel each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49209,
    "dDurationMs": 1831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their wave packets can overlap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51057,
    "dDurationMs": 2314,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, check out this image\nof a ring of iron atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53381,
    "dDurationMs": 1591,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sitting on a surface of copper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54993,
    "dDurationMs": 4054,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see the overlap of the spread out electrons?\nNow, would you call that touching?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59041,
    "dDurationMs": 2196,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at a dictionnary,\ntouch is usually defined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61263,
    "dDurationMs": 3214,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as physical contact.\nWell, contact is defined as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64476,
    "dDurationMs": 2501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "touching physically.\nNot much help."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66988,
    "dDurationMs": 1769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But most of people have\nthis intuitive idea that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68750,
    "dDurationMs": 2177,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "touch is something like two\nsolid objects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70948,
    "dDurationMs": 2061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so close together\nthere is no space between them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73063,
    "dDurationMs": 2446,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The trouble is this doesn't have\nanything to do with overlapping"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75516,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "waves which, as we know,\nare how electrons actually behave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78294,
    "dDurationMs": 2717,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, it seems that touch\nis a word that may just be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81045,
    "dDurationMs": 3255,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incapable of describing the actual\nuniverse as we understand it today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84308,
    "dDurationMs": 2323,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Either that, or we should \nchange our notion of touch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86662,
    "dDurationMs": 2818,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to mean interaction at short distance\nwhich is really what happens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89508,
    "dDurationMs": 2135,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between electrons when you sit on a chair."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91638,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, regardless of whether \nor not we ever actually touch anything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94625,
    "dDurationMs": 2438,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that when we talk about\nthe electromagnetic repulsion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97084,
    "dDurationMs": 2479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your butt and your chair,\nwhat we are really trying to say is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99540,
    "dDurationMs": 2889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey! Remember how cool it is\nthat we are made of atoms and molecules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102414,
    "dDurationMs": 1816,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that other people\nmade of atoms and molecules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104235,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were clever enough \nto figure that out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106108,
    "dDurationMs": 2113,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that is touching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109768,
    "dDurationMs": 3024,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode of Minute Physics\nis supported by audible.com"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112787,
    "dDurationMs": 2848,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The leading provider of audio books\nacross all types of litterature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115673,
    "dDurationMs": 2379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including fiction, non-fiction and periodicals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118089,
    "dDurationMs": 2666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I highly recommend\n'Surely you're joking, Mr. Feynman'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120779,
    "dDurationMs": 2158,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A hilarious and fascinating\nautobiography"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122958,
    "dDurationMs": 2255,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the amazing man and physicist\nRichard Feynman"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125208,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can download this audiobook\nor another of your choice for free"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128119,
    "dDurationMs": 1925,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at audible.com/minutephysics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130081,
    "dDurationMs": 2239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, thanks to Audible\nfor making it possible for me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132314,
    "dDurationMs": 2645,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to keep producing Minute Physics\nand for giving you a free audiobook"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134969,
    "dDurationMs": 3564,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at audible.com/minutephysics"
    } ]
  } ]
}
